From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:58:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] compat: let the build say the kernel already has
 totalram_pages()

compat.h turns totalram_pages() into the old variable for anything older
than 5.0, going by LINUX_VERSION_CODE alone. vince's kernel calls itself
4.9.251 but carries the backport of the atomic counter, where
totalram_pages is a function, so the macro leaves a bare function name:

  ratelimiter.c:187:43: error: invalid operands to binary << (have
  'long unsigned int (*)(void)' and 'int')

The preprocessor cannot see a static inline function, so add a knob the
build can set after looking at the kernel's own mm.h, as for
skb_mark_not_on_list. Kernels that follow the version arithmetic are
unaffected: nothing defines it and the condition is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [upstream is archived; this is vendor-tree specific]
---
--- a/compat/compat.h
+++ b/compat/compat.h
@@ -777,7 +777,11 @@
 #define hlist_add_behind(a, b) hlist_add_after(b, a)
 #endif
 
-#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(5, 0, 0) && !defined(ISRHEL8)
+/* COMPAT_HAVE_TOTALRAM_PAGES_FUNC: set by the build when the kernel's own mm.h
+ * already has totalram_pages() as a function, which an Android vendor tree may
+ * do at a version long before 5.0.
+ */
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(5, 0, 0) && !defined(ISRHEL8) && !defined(COMPAT_HAVE_TOTALRAM_PAGES_FUNC)
 #define totalram_pages() totalram_pages
 #endif
 
